    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "39",
        "end": "39",
        "startOffset": 34,
        "endOffset": 50,
        "text": "you have no idea",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "ENG"
        ]
      },
      "id": "81AA49E5B1",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "39",
        "end": "39",
        "startOffset": 11,
        "endOffset": 89,
        "text": "Thank you all so much, you have no idea how fulfilling and energizing that is.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "1EC3D1D17B",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "40",
        "end": "40",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 131,
        "text": "For the past three years, I've had the privilege of codesigning with my neighbors a space in New Orleans known as Under the Bridge.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "A3AE3DCD0A",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "41",
        "end": "41",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 321,
        "text": "In 1966, Interstate 10 landed on the Tremé neighborhood, displacing 326 black-owned businesses, over 300 live oak trees, effectively destroying the region's most successful black commercial district, disrupting intergenerational wealth and truly unraveling the fabric of the nation's oldest African American neighborhood.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "0C7EBE4939",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "42",
        "end": "42",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 504,
        "text": "Today, after 45 years of community advocacy, after 500 hours of community engagement and 80 hours of community design, we are so excited that in 2018, after capturing the voices of thousands of residents and the support of our local, federal and philanthropic partners, as the city celebrates 300 years of transforming the world, we will get to transform 19 blocks under the Interstate into community space, into black-owned businesses, in the form of the Claiborne Corridor Cultural Innovation District.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "70D8A633C5",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "43",
        "end": "43",
        "startOffset": 31,
        "endOffset": 107,
        "text": "bridging time, we will bridge memory, we will bridge disparity and injustice",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "FIG"
        ]
      },
      "id": "E7CC03D8E0",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "43",
        "end": "43",
        "startOffset": 20,
        "endOffset": 160,
        "text": "We will be bridging time, we will bridge memory, we will bridge disparity and injustice, and we can't wait to see you all on the other side.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "33FC5B183F",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "44",
        "end": "44",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 10,
        "text": "Thank you.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
